 ## Overview
-This method accelerates the cell projection volume rendering technique by using hardware texture mapping to compute the exponential transparency term $\exp(-\int \tau ds)$ per pixel via table lookup, avoiding per-pixel exponential calculations while preventing Mach bands caused by linear interpolation of transparency [S1][S2, unofficial][S3, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from naive cell projection by replacing the linear interpolation of integrated opacity $\alpha$ with a 2D texture lookup that correctly models the non-linear exponential decay of light, which linear interpolation fails to capture [S2, unofficial][S3, unofficial].
