 ## How it works
-The method projects convex polyhedral cells (typically tetrahedra or subdivided hexahedra) onto the image plane, subdividing the projection into polygons where each polygon lies within the projection of a single front-facing face and a single back-facing face [S1][S2, unofficial][S3, unofficial]. For each polygon, the method computes vertex attributes (color, opacity, and texture coordinates) and uses hardware interpolation to rasterize the polygon, applying a pre-loaded texture map to determine the correct per-pixel transparency [S1][S2, unofficial][S3, unofficial].
